WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.670
Blimps are quiet and safe, safe enough for

2
00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:05.850
people to touch without hesitation, but their envelope

3
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.490
has always only been able to display, never

4
00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:08.890
to sense.

5
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.670
What Feelium sets out to solve is making

6
00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.230
the Blimp's skin able to both see and

7
00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:14.530
be touched.

8
00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:17.170
Feelium adds touch sensing to a Blimp's projected

9
00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:17.610
skin.

10
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.350
A camera behind the membrane detects shadows cast

11
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:23.290
by an external press and distinguishes real contact

12
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.810
from a hovering hand by how stable that

13
00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:27.030
shadow stays over time.

14
00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:29.890
Each contact is then classified as a tap,

15
00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.210
a hold, or a swipe based on duration

16
00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:32.610
and movement.

17
00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:35.170
When someone touches the Blimp, a remote person

18
00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.590
wearing VR sees the contact appear on their

19
00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.850
own first-person view and responds by projecting

20
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.450
light back at that location.

21
00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.810
This gives Feelium a two-way touch channel

22
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.450
between a remote person and a co-located

23
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:51.350
partner, applicable to remote visits, daily contact between

24
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.450
distant families and public exhibitions.
